1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,140
Losing collagen faster than you should?

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:09,820
Before you reach for another serum, stop and check three habits that break collagen down faster than any cream can fix.

3
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:11,400
First, smoking.

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:25,600
Cigarette smoke triggers enzymes called MMPs that break down collagen and elastic fibers, and smokers develop two to three times more facial wrinkles than non-smokers the same age.

5
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,540
Second, unprotected sun exposure.

6
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:39,140
UV rays trigger that same collagen-degrading MMP response, and studies show even sun exposure too mild to cause redness is enough to keep that response switched on.

7
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:41,540
Third, a high-sugar diet.

8
00:00:41,860 --> 00:00:50,460
Excess sugar binds to collagen through a process called glycation, forming stiff structures that replace healthy, flexible collagen.

9
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:58,260
Quitting smoking lets collagen levels bounce back — most studies show real improvement within 4 to 8 weeks.

10
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:06,880
Wearing sunscreen daily cuts wrinkle and pigmentation formation by 30 to 50 percent in clinical trials.

11
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:12,960
And cutting back on added sugar slows glycation before it locks in.
